 *   **Performance:** The method avoids the extensive ray sampling of NeRF, maintaining high performance [S1]. It is implemented with custom CUDA kernels for efficiency [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Reduces projection error, leading to higher-quality renderings, especially for Gaussians far from the camera center or at oblique angles [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** The rank-2 handling with matrix $\mathbf{Q}$ is complex and prone to implementation errors due to ambiguities in the source formula [S1]. The per-Gaussian projection plane calculation is more computationally intensive than the global $z=1$ plane [S1].
