 ## Background
-Optimal Gaussian Splatting was introduced in the paper "On the Error Analysis of 3D Gaussian Splatting and an Optimal Projection Strategy" [S1]. It addresses the projection error inherent in the original 3D Gaussian Splatting method, which projects all Gaussians onto a single plane $z=1$ [S1]. The method is based on theoretical error analysis showing that the error is minimized when the projection of the Gaussian mean coincides with the ray direction from the camera center [S1]. It is implemented based on the PyTorch framework and 3D-GS [17] with custom CUDA kernels [S1].
